WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.651
FastAPI is a modern Python framework for
building APIs and web services.

2
00:00:06.731 --> 00:00:12.579
It gives developers a productive path for
defining path operations,

3
00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:18.609
request models, response models,
dependencies, and documentation.

4
00:00:18.689 --> 00:00:21.210
That productivity is useful,

5
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:26.331
but it can also make sensitive behavior
available quickly.

6
00:00:26.411 --> 00:00:32.462
A route that takes only a few lines of
code may still expose account data,

7
00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:37.079
approve business actions, trigger
background work,

8
00:00:37.159 --> 00:00:41.293
or connect internal systems to outside
clients.

9
00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:47.827
Secure FastAPI development means
protecting the full API surface: routes,

10
00:00:47.907 --> 00:00:54.260
request models, dependencies,
authentication, authorization, tokens,

11
00:00:54.340 --> 00:00:59.886
data access, file handling, secrets,
generated documentation,

12
00:00:59.966 --> 00:01:04.705
package dependencies, and deployment
configuration.

13
00:01:04.785 --> 00:01:10.936
It is not only about whether type hints
exist or whether validation runs.

14
00:01:11.016 --> 00:01:18.276
It is about whether the application makes
correct security decisions when inputs are

15
00:01:18.356 --> 00:01:22.994
unexpected, tokens are stale, clients are
untrusted,

16
00:01:23.074 --> 00:01:27.007
or resources belong to another user or
tenant.

17
00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:31.524
It helps to separate responsibility across
layers.

18
00:01:31.604 --> 00:01:34.931
FastAPI provides framework features.

19
00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:40.557
Application logic defines business rules
and access decisions.

20
00:01:40.637 --> 00:01:46.889
Third-party packages add authentication,
data access, serialization,

21
00:01:46.969 --> 00:01:49.692
and operational capabilities.

22
00:01:49.772 --> 00:01:57.334
Infrastructure provides TLS, proxying,
gateways, runtime isolation, and monitoring.

23
00:01:57.414 --> 00:02:04.372
Operations teams handle deployment,
logging, patching, and incident response.

24
00:02:04.452 --> 00:02:11.611
A secure service is built when these
layers reinforce each other instead of assuming

25
00:02:11.691 --> 00:02:15.221
one layer silently solves every problem.

26
00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:22.561
API-first applications are
security-sensitive because they expose business logic

27
00:02:22.641 --> 00:02:28.086
directly to clients, integrations,
services, and automation.

28
00:02:28.166 --> 00:02:33.006
There may be no browser interface hiding
the complexity.

29
00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:36.514
The API contract is the product surface.

30
00:02:36.594 --> 00:02:42.645
Security therefore needs to be designed
into path operations, models,

31
00:02:42.725 --> 00:02:49.178
dependencies, service boundaries, and
operational review from the start.

32
00:02:49.258 --> 00:02:53.292
The goal is repeatable defensive
engineering,

33
00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:59.220
not a one-time hardening pass after the
API is already in production.
